at already have an  account  thank you aransa for those of you that  already have an account especially the  campus ambassadors that are here in this  session  please share your accounts as well  so we will take some account that is  complete so that we can show how a  completed profile looks  okay thank you  all right great so let's take just one  of these accounts as an example  here we have an account by subrajeet who  is already an expert  how do we know that he is an expert  he is an expert first of all because of  the activity that we can already see on  his profile so you can see that all of  your activity as you go through the  lessons as you try different projects as  you try different analysis techniques  are quantified and what that means is  that you get a number of points for  completing each step and that  immediately signals to the mentor  community that you have accomplished the  basic training and you're ready to get  started with your research project so  the way the research fellowship works is  it starts from this basic training  what is covered in the basic training so  importantly i think in today's world  when we speak about bioinformatics the  major focus is on big data  this big data comes in the form of  genomics transcriptomics metagenomics  epigenomics there are many different  types of omics and ultimately you have  to know how to process each individual  types of data and then integrate them  together to really have this systems  level view of what's happening in a  biological condition and so we've  designed these so that you have an  introduction and i will show you a  couple of courses that you can start  with for free so that you get into this  whole field of omics data  then you go through this basic training  and then you get into introduced to the  data science curriculum in r and python  so i will briefly show you a couple  examples and this is just to get you  started  so again as you can see this profile it  is complete with activity i can see  which courses super gene has completed  and i can also see that he has earned  certificates and those certificates are  going to stay with you unless the course  has been updated and when it's updated  your certificate will be  taken away so that you can complete the  remaining lessons and then get the  certificate back and that way we know  that you're staying up to date on some  of these important topics  in addition to that you can participate  in programs and today we're speaking  about the research fellowship program  but also we have many others that are  led by mentors who are experts in the  field and you will also be able to  develop a project so as we go through  one of the requirements that this  program has is so that you complete your  basic training now where would you start  your basic training  here on the courses tab right here in  the menu you can find a lot of courses  that as you work through some of the  material will get a personalized  suggestion for your profile so you can  see that for me i have some suggestions  on single cell transcriptomics machine  learning ebola virus etc and that's  because of my interests  but here below i have a list of  recommended and highly  active courses as well as some of the as  well as some of the  collections of courses that you can find  right here and one of the collections is  called getting started so i can just  click right here on getting started  and see what's included  the course that we recommend for all of  you to start with is a course called  bytes and molecules  the course  explains many of the basic terms  bytes  so  a lot of the basic terms that you need  to know to get into this field and it is  using you know language that anyone can  understand both  with and without  the kind of bioinformatics background  and it covers important topics that you  will want to understand before you  really get into a lot of the material  that is related to research using  bioinformatics so that's just where you  would want to start with  so after you complete  enough material to generate 10 000  points what will be made available  is right here  under projects you will be able to start  a new project and that is essentially  what this program is all about so this  program is going to be  focused on getting beyond the training  after you've completed the 10 000 points  and into a research topic now one of the  immediate challenges with that is how do  you process this huge amount of data  that oftentimes is beyond several  gigabytes or even terabytes of data that  you have to download on your computer  and so for that we specifically designed  a big data analysis platform that will  cover many of the typical processing  steps that reduce the amount of data  from gigabytes and terabytes to just  megabytes which is possible to analyze  either on your system or in the cloud  and we will introduce you to cloud  technologies using this platform called  the t violin for platform developed at  the caliber bioinformatics research  center at university of haifa as well as  some of the cloud technologies offered  by other companies like google co-lab  github and other resources that are  going to be useful for you to leverage  as you develop your career in  bioinformatics  so here we have i'll just briefly show  you one example as you probably all know  transcriptomic data data on rna  sequencing is becoming more and more  prominent in many different areas of  research including oncology  neuroscience and other fields and  briefly you can appreciate the  simplicity of this platform because it  really organizes the information in a  logical step-by-step process and by the  way this is reflected in the coursework  that you will find on the learn portal  it also guides you using artificial  intelligence based on the data that you  upload and the information that you  would like to receive from this pipeline  so that you can eliminate the common  mistakes that people make when they try  to design these  workflows on their own  now as a result of running these  workflows you also get a clear sense of  the logic behind the analysis including  the inputs and outputs of different  methods and so once you're ready to  transition to your own independent  pipeline that you want to build on your  own now you at least understand the  logic why would i use this method and  not that method when would i try to  modify this setting or that setting and  this spans as i mentioned across many  different areas of analysis including  next generation sequencing data mass  spectroscopy  structural biology as well as many  methods for data integration and  modeling machine learning and other  types of applications so all of you can  definitely go through some of these  resources the thing is once you've  created an account on the onixler  omixlogic portal you automatically get  access to the demo level on this  bioinformatics platform after 24 hours  so from the moment that you created a  profile today tomorrow morning you can  already start using this platform seeing  how it is used in different courses and  projects that we will talk about  so this is the t binary platform  now ultimately you're probably wondering  well okay i have these resources i can  go through the training i can understand  what topic i would like to analyze it i  can perform the analysis but how do i  know that i'm doing the right thing  and so to do that we have a community of  mentors and i think that's a very  critical point to  briefly discuss  so our community of mentors first of all  is an international community many of  our  mentors come from research backgrounds  many of them have a phd  in a particular domain like  bioinformatics computational biology  neuroscience oncology etc and today you  will hear from some of them  but also many of them come with industry  experience and so for those of you that  understand what you want to do with your  career if you would like to go beyond  basic research and focus on  translational research projects that is  one of the  specific goals of this program as well  as a research fellow you get to explore  a variety of topics and select one that  is either relevant for industry or for  research and we'll talk about this today  including different collaborations that  we have with universities and  organizations that provide us with this  opportunity to know what is needed and  is in demand at the cutting edge of  basic research and industry r d as well  so what are some of the outcomes the  outcomes of this program is that you  will come out knowing  how to apply bioinformatics to a  particular project and you will be able  to complete that project within a short  period of time and just to give you a  sense of what i mean by that i want to  pass this presentation now to dr  harpreet kapoor


